    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d174">

                <pb facs="0221" n="1055" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg1055"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9815</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-09-05T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 5, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1195. For Sheldon [from
                    War Trade Board]:</p>
                <p>No. 1165. Frothingham. Embassy’s 1178, August 19, 1 p.m.,
                    your 1259.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d174-f1"/> Conference here has determined
                    advisable that conference plan extend to all cases other than those excepted in
                    original proposition by War Trade Board embodied in despatch July 1.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d174-f2"/> This result has been communicated to French
                    authorities through McFadden and recommended to French authorities through French
                    representative, Washington. Italians make proposal to agree conference plan to
                    extent of persons on refusal lists but not other enemy persons. Washington
                    conference including Italian representative agree desirable conference plan be
                    adopted in full by all governments represented by conferees. This result
                    communicated Italian authorities through Stewart at Rome and
                    recommended to Italian authorities by Italian representative in Washington. Act
                    pending final agreement according instructions our 1133, Aug. 27 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">31</hi>], and despatch August 30.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d174-f3"/> Hereafter in cabling reference enemy trade license
                    conference do not mark cable for Fuller but simply send as War Trade Board cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
